            <div xml:id="d435">

                <pb facs="0428" n="416" sameAs="frus:frus1943v04/pg416"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.01/93: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Iran</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Ford</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tehran</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-12-15T12:00:00+03:25">December 15,
                            1943—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 12:44 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1122. Prime Minister Soheily resigned yesterday. It is thought this is merely a
                    tactical move to enable him to eliminate certain members of Cabinet and that
                    Shah will request him to form a new government in next few days. Soheily has
                    been talking of a reorganization for months but has apparently been unable
                    persuade men concerned to resign.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ford</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
